  "prediction": "**Summary of USAID Assistance to the West Bank and Gaza**\n\nThe United States Agency for International Development (USAID) has obligated over $5 billion in bilateral assistance to the Palestinians in the West Bank and Gaza since 1993. The majority of this assistance was provided through the Economic Support Fund (ESF) and was used to support various development objectives, including economic growth, infrastructure development, health, education, and governance.\n\nAs of March 31, 2018, USAID had obligated approximately $544.1 million (over 99 percent) and expended about $350.6 million (over 64 percent) of the $544.5 million allocated for the West Bank and Gaza in fiscal years 2015 and 2016. The assistance was used to support projects in areas such as private sector development, health, water and sanitation, and education.\n\nUSAID also made direct payments to Palestinian Authority (PA) creditors totaling about $75 million in fiscal year 2015 and $70 million in fiscal year 2016. These payments were made to ensure that the PA's creditors were paid and to minimize the risk of misuse of funds.\n\nTo ensure that assistance did not inadvertently support terrorism, USAID implemented antiterrorism policies and procedures, including vetting of PA creditors and external assessments of the PA's financial systems. The agency also commissioned financial audits of the debt relief grants to ensure that funds were used as intended.\n\nThe report concludes that USAID has taken steps to ensure that assistance to the West Bank and Gaza is used effectively and efficiently, and that the agency has complied with relevant laws and regulations. However, the report also notes that there are ongoing challenges in the region, including the need for continued support for economic development and governance.\n\n**Key Findings:**\n\n* USAID has obligated over $5 billion in assistance to the West Bank and Gaza since 1993.\n* The majority of this assistance was provided through the ESF and was used to support various development objectives.\n* USAID made direct payments to PA creditors totaling about $75 million in fiscal year 2015 and $70 million in fiscal year 2016.\n* USAID implemented antiterrorism policies and procedures to ensure that assistance did not inadvertently support terrorism.\n* The agency commissioned financial audits of the debt relief grants to ensure that funds were used as intended.\n\n**Recommendations:**\n\n* USAID should continue to provide assistance to the West Bank and Gaza to support economic development and governance.\n* The agency should continue to implement antiterrorism",
